{quote}Do we need to delete or anonymise the data in Jumio/Veriff?{quote}

In theory we should (with the caveat below). afaik this would require sending a request to their support.

{quote}Since the driving licence data is also stored in Admin, should this information be deleted as well?{quote}

yes with the caveat below.

{quote}Shouldn’t there be cases when we should keep the user’s data to prevent fraud? For example, a user who had been temporarily or permanently blocked asks to delete their account and driving licence data. After that, they register a new account, possibly with the same name and phone number. Without past data, we cannot know and prevent such users from performing illegal/fraudulent activities again.{quote}

absolutely, there should be a process to not delete any data if there is a fraud or debt risk. also deletion should not be immediate to prevent future issues. we should probably have a process here like “wait 90 days then delete”. 

When all the data goes through the Verification Platform we will be able to handle all of this as part of the standard account deletion requests, but we havent built out this capability yet.

{quote}*If the user still has an active account and requests to delete their driving licence data:*

Do we need to decline such request and explain to the user that this data is required to provide the Bolt Drive service?{quote}

You can delete it but then they will be unable to use Drive without adding it again.

{quote}In Veriff, all driving licence verifications (except ones that were created and sent to the user manually by our CS) are automatically deleted after 3 months. Should this data be communicated to the user in the T&C or elsewhere? Should we share this with the user who has an active account but requested to delete their DL data?{quote}

No, this is specific to Veriff and shouldn't be communicated externally as it’s subject to change and not under our control.

